# Brand constraints

A brand is not merely a logo, color palette, font pairing, gradient, or collection of components. It is a coherent world that remains recognizable when the logo is hidden.

Project-specific identity decisions may not yet exist. Derive them through the creative-direction workflow (`creative-director`, `brand-world-builder`) and record them in design memory. Do not invent and ship identity decisions without documenting them.

## Required reading

Before material visual or verbal changes:

- `.cursor/design-memory/approved-direction.md`
- `.cursor/design-memory/visual-decisions.md`
- `.cursor/design-memory/creative-thesis.md`

## What must stay consistent once approved

Preserve approved decisions for:

| Domain | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| Central brand metaphor | The governing image or idea |
| Emotional territory | How the product should feel |
| Brand attributes | Adjectives that constrain choices |
| Color relationships | Not just hex values; how colors behave |
| Typography | Display, reading, interface, numeric roles |
| Logo behavior | Clearspace, minimum size, forbidden treatments |
| Graphic devices | Recurring visual motifs |
| Image treatment | Crop, grade, grain, contrast |
| Illustration system | Style, line weight, perspective |
| Icon language | Stroke, corner, metaphor level |
| Surface hierarchy | Background, elevated, inset, accent |
| Shape language | Radius, chamfer, cut, overlap |
| Motion language | Easing, duration, what moves vs. stays still |
| Voice | Tone, compression, confidence level |
| Vocabulary | Words the brand owns or avoids |
| Product screenshots | Frame, shadow, context, annotation |
| Data visualization | Chart personality, color logic |
| State surfaces | Empty, loading, success, warning, error |

## Change control

- Document any approved change in `.cursor/design-memory/visual-decisions.md` using the decision log format.
- Do not silently change previously approved design principles.
- When superseding a decision, keep the old entry and mark it superseded with reason and date.
- If `approved-direction.md` status is "Not yet approved," creative exploration is open. Once approved, deviations require explicit documentation.

## Marketing and product unity

Marketing pages and the application share:

- Typography hierarchy logic
- Color relationships (adjusted for density)
- Motion personality
- Voice and vocabulary
- Graphic devices and shape language

They differ in:

- Information density
- Pacing and narrative vs. task focus
- Decorative vs. functional emphasis

The product UI must not become a decorative marketing page. The marketing site must not become a generic landing template.

## Copy alignment

Visual brand constraints work with `draper-honeycopy.mdc` and `voice-and-boundaries.mdc`. Copy and visuals must express the same central idea. Invoke `brand-copy-director` when voice and layout diverge.

## Logo-hidden test

Before approving a direction, verify: cover the logo. Is the page still recognizably fajita-io? If not, strengthen composition, type, color behavior, or signature devices before building more pages.
